    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 121124\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n424 AM PDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n*  Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts expected across the region \n   Friday through the weekend. Continued dry conditions with these \n   winds will lead to fire danger.\n\n*  Temperatures cool through the weekend.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Thursday\n\nAfter hazardously hot conditions from a strong high pressure, the \npattern finally changes into Saturday. A trough is deepening over the \nPacific Northwest and push inland and south into Saturday. This will \nhelp shift the the high pressure eastward, but the space between \nthese systems will narrow, leading to a stronger pressure gradient \nand increasing winds. Breezy winds build through Saturday morning \nand will peak that afternoon with widespread gusts above 30 mph \npossible and above 40 mph in higher terrain and within favored gaps \nand passes. This coupled with very dry conditions will increase fire \nweather concerns. Fire Red Flag Warning will go in effect at 11 AM \nfor Esmeralda, Nye, and portions of Lincoln and Clark counties and \nwill last into late Saturday night. Winds look to reduce for Sunday \nbut remain breezy. Longer term models keep breezy winds peaking \naround 25 mph each afternoon into the first half of next week, but \nwinds look to ease in the late week.\n\nAs the high pressure pushes east and focuses over Texas,\ntemperatures (both highs and lows) will begin to decrease through \nthe weekend. High temps will fall back to around average (90s to \nlow 100s) before the work week. Low temperatures will see some \nreduction, but will plateau in the early work week, and stay \naround 5 degrees above average. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...A \nlull in gusty winds may occur early this morning before winds \nstrengthen and shift to the southwest by mid morning, with sustained \nspeeds over 10 knots and gusts between 20 and 25 knots. Winds start \nto decrease in the evening but remain gusty through tonight and into \ntomorrow morning, possibly including a lull between midnight and \nsunrise. FEW high clouds will filter through the area. Temperatures \nexceed 100 degrees between 20Z and 02Z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...South to southwest winds \nwill intensify later this morning and afternoon, with gusts around \n25 knots in the Las Vegas Valley and around 20 knots in the Colorado \nRiver Valley. Winds favor a more westerly direction at KDAG. Gusty \nwinds weaken slightly after sunset but last into the evening as \nwell. FEW to SCT mid and high clouds will filter through the area.\n\n&&\n\n.FIRE WEATHER...A Red Flag Warning and is in effect from 11AM \nSaturday through midnight for Nye, Esmeralda, and portions of \nLincoln and Clark counties. Concerns include RH ranging from 5 to \n15% while winds increase to 25 MPH and gusts to around 35 MPH. \nWinds will continue into the overnight as humidities begin to \nrecover by late that night. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Murdock\nAVIATION...Meltzer\nFIRE WEATHER...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
